# DTF tier manifest: virtual-member-fallback-strict
#   (artifact-keeper#5810, PR #5892; main only, for 1.12.0)
# Profile-set: filesystem + a run-time-filled upstream (upstreams.mock-files:
# a stdlib-python server on 172.16.<slot>.76 whose files the oracle writes over
# a control API). One mock stands in for every Remote member: each member's
# upstream URL is its own path prefix. The oracle makes a member hang by
# holding its paths (POST /__delay, 120 s, longer than the 60 s upstream read
# timeout and the 20 s download deadline).
#
# THE CHANGE (#5810)
#   Since #5845 (download deadline) and #5849 (member breaker), a download
#   through a Virtual passes over an unavailable Remote member and serves the
#   next member's copy. Two members can hold different content at the same
#   coordinates, so #5892 adds a per-virtual setting `virtual_member_fallback`
#   (`available`, the default, or `strict`). In strict mode the first member in
#   priority order that is unavailable ends the download with 503 and
#   Retry-After. A hung member costs the download deadline (20 s by default),
#   not the upstream read timeout (PROXY_UPSTREAM_READ_TIMEOUT_SECS, 60 s). A
#   404 is still a miss.
#
# THE GATES
#   (FIX)      RED on ghcr main (no setting: it is not stored or reported, and
#              a strict virtual serves the lower member's copy after the
#              deadline). GREEN on main + #5892.
#              #5810 the setting is stored and read back (`strict` on the
#                    strict virtual, `available` on an untouched one), and an
#                    unknown value or a non-virtual is refused with 400;
#              #5810 strict virtual [hung remote, healthy remote]: a Maven
#                    jar download answers 503 + Retry-After inside 45 s (the
#                    20 s deadline, not the 60 s read timeout), with none of
#                    the lower member's bytes;
#              #5810 strict Docker virtual [5xx remote, healthy remote]: an
#                    OCI manifest pull by tag (`/v2/<virtual>/app/manifests/
#                    latest`) answers 503 + Retry-After, not the lower
#                    member's manifest.
#   (CONTROL)  must hold on BOTH images:
#              default virtual [hung remote, healthy remote] serves the lower
#              member's jar 200 inside 45 s; strict virtual [404 remote,
#              healthy remote] serves the lower member's jar (a 404 is a
#              miss); strict virtual [healthy remote, healthy remote] serves
#              the top member's jar; default Docker virtual [5xx remote,
#              healthy remote] serves the lower member's manifest by tag.
#
# TIMING: two downloads wait out the default 20 s download deadline
# (AK_VIRTUAL_MEMBER_DOWNLOAD_DEADLINE_SECS); each allows 45 s, and curl
# allows 75 s so a wait for the full read timeout is measured, not cut off.
#
# RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=false: ~40 requests back to back.
# UPSTREAM_ALLOW_PRIVATE_IPS=true: the mock upstream is on a private subnet.
COVERS="5810"
PROFILES="storage.filesystem upstreams.mock-files"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
UPSTREAM_ALLOW_PRIVATE_IPS="true"
